NEARS-3520 AC1 — live device (emulator-5556) attempt log, DeliveryApp built off
worktree HEAD 8b00dd6d4, logged in as delivery_man td@td.com (id 5, payable
balance 66.00 AED).

Flow driven live: Dashboard -> "ادفع الآن" (Pay Now) -> My Account/Wallet ->
"ادفع الآن" -> payment method bottom sheet -> selected each of the two
available gateways ("Paypal", "Razor pay") in turn.

Observed via app log (flutter run stdout) + `adb logcat`:

1. POST /api/v1/delivery-man/make-collected-cash-payment -> http_status=200
   (redirect_link generated: http://10.0.2.2:8000/payment/{gateway}/pay/?payment_id=<uuid>)
2. InAppBrowser opens; the initial navigation to OUR OWN backend host loads
   and renders successfully — NOT canceled (correct: same host as baseUrl is
   allow-listed). No "payment webview navigation blocked" log line fired for
   this legitimate navigation (confirms zero false-positive blocking of the
   real payment flow — the fix does not regress the happy path).
3. Paypal path: page rendered JSON `{"response_code":"gateways_default_204",...}`
   — PaypalPaymentController fails closed to this generic response because
   business_settings.paypal has null client_id/secret in this local dev DB
   (confirmed via `SELECT value FROM business_settings WHERE key='paypal'` ->
   {"status":"0","paypal_client_id":null,"paypal_secret":null}). No external
   navigation to paypal.com is ever attempted — the flow terminates on our own
   host before any redirect decision is needed.
4. Razor Pay path: page rendered the razor-pay Blade view, which loads
   `https://checkout.razorpay.com/v1/checkout.js` as a SUBRESOURCE (<script
   src>, not a top-level navigation — chromium console line confirms:
   "source: https://checkout.razorpay.com/v1/checkout.js"). This is correctly
   NOT subject to shouldOverrideUrlLoading (that gate only fires on
   navigation actions, not resource fetches) and is NOT blocked — expected,
   since blocking subresource loads would break the checkout widget itself.
   The widget then failed client-side with console error "Error creating
   order: Error: No key passed" (business_settings.razor_pay also has null
   razor_key/razor_secret) — again terminating without any external
   top-level navigation, confirmed via `adb logcat` chromium CONSOLE lines.
5. Backing out of both attempts (`_exitApp` -> "Cancel Payment") returned
   cleanly to the My Account screen both times — no crash, 0 runtime errors
   (`ui_errors` scanned 124-126 flutter-tag lines for the app's own pid across
   the whole session, 0 matches).

ENVIRONMENT CONSTRAINT (not a fix defect): both gateways configured/selectable
in this local dev DB (Paypal, Razor Pay) have null sandbox credentials, and the
DM "collect cash payment" endpoint's own `Payment::generate_link()` only ever
returns a URL on OUR OWN backend host (`url("payment/{gateway}/pay/...")`) — a
genuine cross-host top-level redirect (the exact scenario shouldOverrideUrlLoading's
host-block guards against) could not be organically triggered via the real
business flow in this environment, because no gateway integration here is wired
with live/sandbox credentials capable of completing a checkout and redirecting
back. This is confirmed structural (verified by reading
PaypalPaymentController::payment()/RazorPayController::index() and the
business_settings rows directly), not a gap introduced or left open by this
ticket. The negative control (host-block itself firing) is instead demonstrated
deterministically via the live re-run of payment_webview_host_allowlist_test.dart
(ac1-unit-tests-rerun.log in this same evidence dir), which exercises the exact
production `PaymentWebViewHostAllowlist.isAllowedHost`/`MyInAppBrowser.matchesSuccessFlag`
static methods `shouldOverrideUrlLoading`/`_redirect` call — not a mock.
